What was changed
----------------
- The ShaderDesk engine wrapper was removed. scene_bake and scene_frame became one
  mainImage(); the uniforms became iResolution and iTime. The picture is laid out
  in display heights from fragCoord, as in the original.
- noise.png (iChannel0) replaces the original's baked texture. It holds the same
  seamlessly tiling fBm as the red, green and blue channels of scene_bake (24 x 16
  cells, 768 x 512 pixels, 8 bits), made once by running the same hash and noise
  maths from Scenes/Common.metal. It is a generated image, not taken from anywhere.
- The starfield that the original bakes into the texture's alpha channel is
  computed per pixel with the same star layers, as if on a display 1000 points high.
- The scene clock is iTime wrapped at 1200 s; every period in the scene divides it,
  so the wrap cannot be seen.
- ShaderDesk's shared bloom pass and dithering are not available. The tone map and
  the sRGB encoding that ShaderDesk applies at the end are done in mainImage().
- The helper functions hash11, hash12, hash22, noise1 and starLayer were copied from
  Scenes/Common.metal of the same repository (starLayer keeps only the intensity,
  which is all this scene used). The per-display seed and the brightness setting
  are fixed at 0 and 1.
- Colours, shapes, step counts and speeds are unchanged.

